ID: vr-46
Title: Independent default-on Always on top for every popped-out head

Status: DONE
Milestone: Every managed model keeps identity/topmost in its floating menu, initially pinned.
Dependencies: vr-45

Purpose:
Keep each opted-in chat head above normal application windows by default,
with an independent toggle inside the head's collapsible menu and in the
single manager. Keep the head name inside that menu too, not a bottom badge.

Tasks:
[x] Preserve native pin IPC and enable named-head pinning by default.
[x] Expose the same control on all six managed models, including native MPFB.
[x] Hide pin/name inside the existing collapsed menu; native details fallback for MPFB.
[x] Qualify default native topmost state, toggling and independent ownership.
[x] Update chapter/guide/index/ledger, issue/Project and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
New managed heads default to native always-on-top. Their menu checkbox and
manager setting operate the same per-head control without regenerating speech.
Pin/name are not visible with the menu collapsed. Central manager pinning
remains available while that menu is closed.
Turning off one head's pin leaves another head's pin unchanged.
Existing owner sessions/profiles are not reloaded, restarted or driven.
Secure desktops, exclusive fullscreen and ordering between competing topmost
windows are not promised; no global window policy or startup service.

Completion evidence:
topmost-controls-02/controls-report.json: actual common module in isolated
Electron using real Claire toolbar/CSS and native MPFB CSS. Checked default,
pin/name hidden when collapsed, expand/re-collapse, reused original listener,
direct click and manager update while hidden, one pin control per head.
topmost-native-02/topmost-report.json: two actual Claire/MPFB heads have
WS_EX_TOPMOST by default; off/on through the manager changes only that native
window. Other head stays pinned. Owned manager stopped/descriptors removed.
Six targeted CPU session cases and five Node bridge/player cases pass.
No new dependency/device, new speech, listening or human visual acceptance.
Protected user lane at inspection: manager Python191968 and head Python196224
with their launchers190892/173368; do not touch/reload/stop these processes.
Candidate source starts from8be8753, uses own profiles/data and exact owned PIDs.

Completion log:
2026-11-21 - Owner explicitly requests an Always on top option on the separate
head and then requires enabled by default. Existing native pin IPC is reusable;
